{"task_id": "HumanEval/120", "solution": "def maximum(arr, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array arr of integers and a positive integer k, return a sorted list\n    of length k with the maximum k numbers in arr.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Sort the array in descending order and take the first k elements\n    # Then sort these k elements in ascending order as required by the problem.\n    arr.sort(reverse=True)\n    result = arr[:k]\n    result.sort()\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/118", "solution": "def get_closest_vowel(word):\n    \"\"\"You are given a word. Your task is to find the closest vowel that stands between\n    two consonants from the right side of the word (case sensitive).\n\n    Vowels in the beginning and ending doesn't count. Return empty string if you didn't\n    find any vowel met the above condition.\n\n    You may assume that the given string contains English letter only.\n\n    Example:\n    get_closest_vowel(\"yogurt\") ==> \"u\"\n    get_closest_vowel(\"FULL\") ==> \"U\"\n    get_closest_vowel(\"quick\") ==> \"\"\n    get_closest_vowel(\"ab\") ==> \"\"\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_vowel(char):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a character is a vowel (case-sensitive).\"\"\"\n        return char in \"aeiouAEIOU\"\n\n    def _is_consonant(char):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a character is a consonant (case-sensitive).\"\"\"\n        return char.isalpha() and not _is_vowel(char)\n\n    n = len(word)\n    # Iterate from the second to the second-to-last character\n    # This excludes vowels at the beginning and end as per requirements\n    for i in range(n - 2, 0, -1):\n        char = word[i]\n        prev_char = word[i-1]\n        next_char = word[i+1]\n\n        if _is_vowel(char) and _is_consonant(prev_char) and _is_consonant(next_char):\n            return char\n\n    return \"\""}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/117", "solution": "def select_words(s, n):\n    \"\"\"Given a string s and a natural number n, you have been tasked to implement\n    a function that returns a list of all words from string s that contain exactly\n    n consonants, in order these words appear in the string s.\n    If the string s is empty then the function should return an empty list.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_consonant(char):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a single character is a consonant, ignoring case.\"\"\"\n        char_lower = char.lower()\n        return 'a' <= char_lower <= 'z' and char_lower not in 'aeiou'\n\n    def _count_consonants(word):\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of consonants in a given word.\"\"\"\n        count = 0\n        for char in word:\n            if _is_consonant(char):\n                count += 1\n        return count\n\n    def _split_into_words(text):\n        \"\"\"Splits an input string into a list of individual words.\"\"\"\n        return text.split()\n\n    if not s:\n        return []\n\n    words = _split_into_words(s)\n    result = []\n    for word in words:\n        if _count_consonants(word) == n:\n            result.append(word)\n    return result"}
